<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Eastern Hungarian Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1526 CE – 1570 CE · capital Buda; later Gyulafehérvár</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Rival Hungarian kingdom of John Zápolya and his son, backed by the Ottomans, which became the seed of the Principality of Transylvania.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ii-of-hungary">Louis II</a> died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mohacs">Mohács</a> in 1526, the Hungarian nobility split. A diet at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szekesfehervar">Székesfehérvár</a> crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-zapolya">John Zápolya</a>, voivode of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-transylvania">Transylvania</a>, in November 1526, while a rival diet chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-holy-roman-emperor">Ferdinand of Habsburg</a>. Driven out by Ferdinand in 1527, Zápolya accepted the protection of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Sultan Suleiman</a>, who restored him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buda">Buda</a> in 1529.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom held the eastern half of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-transylvania">Transylvania</a> under Ottoman suzerainty. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-zapolya">Zápolya</a>'s death in 1540, his widow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabella-jagiellon">Isabella Jagiellon</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-martinuzzi">George Martinuzzi</a> governed for the infant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-sigismund-zapolya">John Sigismund</a>. When Suleiman seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buda">Buda</a> in 1541, the court moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alba-iulia">Gyulafehérvár</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-torda">Diet of Torda</a> in 1568 proclaimed broad religious freedom.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>By the Treaty of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-speyer">Speyer</a> in 1570, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-sigismund-zapolya">John Sigismund</a> gave up the title of king and was recognised as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-transylvania">Prince of Transylvania</a>, turning the realm into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-transylvania">Principality of Transylvania</a>. The division between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-habsburg">Habsburg</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hungary-1526-1867">Royal Hungary</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-hungary">Ottoman Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> lasted until the late 17th century.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/eastern-hungarian-kingdom.jpg" alt="Eastern Hungarian Kingdom" width="320" height="226"><figcaption>Image: Fz22 at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eastern-hungarian-kingdom1550.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1526 CE – 1570 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Buda; later Gyulafehérvár</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>John Zápolya, Isabella Jagiellon, John Sigismund Zápolya</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic and Protestant Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hungarian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a>, <a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of John Zápolya, Szapolyai Hungary</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1548&amp;focus=eastern-hungarian-kingdom" aria-label="Eastern Hungarian Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5125 513 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Eastern Hungarian Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5445 769L5446 783M5445 769L5709 970M5445 769L5464 811"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5446 783h0M5709 970h0M5464 811h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5445 769h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5445 769h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Buda. <a href="/atlas?year=1548&amp;focus=eastern-hungarian-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
